# VERITAS-600 Cursor Rules

You are working on VERITAS-600, a high-reliability Neuro-Symbolic Trade Finance & UCP 600 Adjudication Engine.

## Prime Directives
1. Always check STATUS.md before and after your tasks.
2. Maintain strict separation between deterministic math and neural legal judgment.
3. Hard Invariant Rule: A neural LLM verdict can NEVER override a failed deterministic check.
4. Python deterministic engines handle:
   - Calendar math & date checks (UCP 600 Art. 6(d)(i), 14(c), 20(a)(ii)).
   - 5-banking-day examination clock (Art. 14(b) & Art. 16).
   - Tolerances & amounts (+/- 5% under Art. 30(b), invoice limit under Art. 18(b)).
   - Insurance calculations: >= 110% of CIF/CIP (Art. 28(f)(ii)) and Cover Note rejection (Art. 28(c)).
   - Physical weight reconciliations across documents (Art. 14(d)).
5. Neural LLMs (NVIDIA Nemotron) handle ONLY:
   - Lexical & semantic judgment of typographical errors (ISBP 745 Para A23).
   - General vs specific goods descriptions (UCP 600 Art. 14(e) vs 18(c)).
   - Address variations on transport documents (UCP 600 Art. 14(j)).
6. Database Federation (Zetaris):
   - Always pre-aggregate amendments and watchlist hits into CTEs before joining lc_master.
   - Exactly 1 row per LC must be returned (no row multiplication).
7. Final Actions:
   - Distinguish documentary refusal (SWIFT MT734) from regulatory freeze (AML/Sanctions Compliance Hold).
   - Always gate final bank action behind the Human Examiner Sign-Off button.
